config RVM_GUEST
	bool "RVM guest port"
	depends on CPU_CORTEX_M
	depends on !SMP
	depends on !USERSPACE
	depends on !ARM_MPU
	depends on !CORTEX_M_SYSTICK
	depends on !TICKLESS_KERNEL
	depends on !GEN_ISR_TABLES
	depends on !THREAD_LOCAL_STORAGE
	help
	  Build Zephyr as an unprivileged RVM guest on ARMv7-M.  The RVM
	  monitor owns the physical vector table, SVC, PendSV, SysTick and
	  the NVIC; this port replaces the normal Cortex-M reset, exception
	  and interrupt paths with the RVM virtual vector ABI.  The port
	  supports basic and FPU-extended exception frames; the unsupported
	  options above would silently corrupt the frame, leave the TLS
	  pointer stale, or bypass the RVM interrupt model.
